Rule 1 (output tensor must have the same shape as input)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (suppress complex-to-bool cast when out is provided)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10) ∨ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 3 (float inputs keep the same dtype in out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∧ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
>>
Rule 4 (integral inputs use a floating output dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 2 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 3 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 4 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 5) ∨ (dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8)
>>
Rule 5 (complex inputs preserve complex dtype in out)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10)
>>
